----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE — what shipped (parity with the web source)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The web `WidgetStatGrid` is a PURE presentational widget primitive (a shared widget building block): it
  takes `stats: StatGridItem[]` + optional `compact` / `cols` and renders a responsive grid of `<StatCard>`s.
  Each StatCard = a muted label + optional icon, the bold value with an optional muted unit affix, and an
  optional direction-aware trend chip (web `↑`/`↓`/`—` glyph + value; colored green when `positive`
  (= `trend === 'up'`), muted when `flat`, else red). The column count is `compact ? 1 : (cols ??
  autoCols(stats.length))`, where `autoCols` = `len % 3 → 3 / len % 4 → 4 / else 2`; the inter-item gap is
  `compact ? gap-2 (8) : gap-3 (12)`. Its only own branch is `stats.length === 0 -> <EmptyState
  message="No stats available" />`.
  There is NO fetch / React-Query / Promise in the source, so it has NO loading/error/stale/offline branch
  (the host widget that owns the query renders those). Per the sibling presentational-primitive precedent
  (Delta 0081, MetricCard 0095, WidgetComparisonCard 0003) this surface reproduces ONLY the source's REAL
  branches — inventing loading/error/stale/offline chrome would fabricate states the source does not have:
    • populated grid   (one cell per stat, laid out in the resolved column count; web stats.map(...))
    • compact collapse  (single column + condensed gap; web `compact ? 1` / `gap-2`)
    • explicit cols     (web `cols ?? autoCols`); auto column table (web autoCols)
    • empty leaf        (friendly "never a blank box" peer of web <EmptyState message="No stats available"/>)
  The web `valueColor?: string` className passthrough is modeled as a theme-aware semantic `StatValueTone`
  (no Tailwind ports), exactly as MetricCard (0095) maps the web `neonColorMap[color]` to design tokens.
  Files: WidgetStatGrid.Adapter/Model/.swift/Views/Previews/AdapterTests/Tests.swift + .strings.
  Bindings : P1/S8 WidgetStatGridModel @Observable holder (props + projection; no HTTP in the view);
             P1/S9 tokens (Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius) — no Tailwind ports, no raw hex;
             P1/S10 NSLocalizedString facade (table "WidgetStatGrid"); P1/S11 view.opened telemetry
             (slug "WidgetStatGrid", emitted once + idempotent across appear/disappear).
  i18n     : web source has 0 t() keys (anonymous; its only literal "No stats available" is reproduced via
             widgetStatGrid.empty). Native a11y/HIG additions: emptyHint, cellLabel, valueUnit, trend,
             cellTrend, trendUp/trendDown/trendFlat. 0 dead keys; 0 hardcoded English in Swift.
  a11y     : each cell folds label+value(+unit)+trend into one VoiceOver element ("{label}, {value}{unit},
             {direction} {magnitude}"); the trend arrow + icon are decorative and hidden from VoiceOver
             (direction spoken as a word); empty leaf is one combined element; Dynamic Type via tokens;
             high-contrast via the dynamic token colors.

